1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:03,032
Fourteen facts that sound wrong, but are true.

2
00:00:03,782 --> 00:00:07,555
Water expands when it freezes, which is why ice floats on a lake.

3
00:00:08,105 --> 00:00:12,494
A light-year is the distance light travels in one year, not a measure of time.

4
00:00:13,044 --> 00:00:16,260
The human body contains about thirty-seven trillion cells.

5
00:00:16,810 --> 00:00:19,225
Sound cannot travel through the vacuum of space.

6
00:00:19,775 --> 00:00:23,177
Photosynthesis converts light energy into chemical energy.

7
00:00:23,727 --> 00:00:27,291
The Earth's core is roughly as hot as the surface of the Sun.

8
00:00:27,841 --> 00:00:32,833
Antibiotic resistance arises when bacteria evolve under selective pressure.

9
00:00:33,383 --> 00:00:37,179
A black hole's event horizon is the boundary beyond which nothing can escape.

10
00:00:37,729 --> 00:00:42,791
Honey never spoils; edible honey has been found in three-thousand-year-old Egyptian tombs.

11
00:00:43,341 --> 00:00:45,849
Octopuses have three hearts and blue blood.

12
00:00:46,399 --> 00:00:49,127
A day on Venus is longer than a year on Venus.

13
00:00:49,677 --> 00:00:52,254
Bananas are berries, but strawberries are not.

14
00:00:52,804 --> 00:00:54,754
Sharks existed before trees.

15
00:00:55,304 --> 00:00:59,054
A teaspoon of neutron star material would weigh billions of tons.

16
00:00:59,604 --> 00:01:04,074
Which one surprised you? Tell me in the comments, and follow for more science.

